% The transitive closure of an eight-node chain: the program PLAN.md
% section 11 measures the two engines on.  Its twin, eval-naive-scans, is the
% same source under -D naive, and both pin the counters -v prints, so a
% change in either engine's work fails a case instead of passing quietly.
%
% Each engine derives the same 28 path rows.  Semi-naive reads 287 tuples
% against naive's 398, which is the reduction spec §41 exists for.
% Iterations move the other way -- 7 against 3 -- and that is not a
% regression: a naive pass is not one step of the closure, because join()
% re-reads the inner literal's relation size for every outer row and so picks
% up what the same pass has just derived.  A delta round cannot, since its
% designated literal scans a delta that is fixed for the round.
edge(1, 2).
edge(2, 3).
edge(3, 4).
edge(4, 5).
edge(5, 6).
edge(6, 7).
edge(7, 8).

path(X, Y) :-
	edge(X, Y).

path(X, Z) :-
	path(X, Y),
	edge(Y, Z).
